<h2>Catechist Guide</h2>
<p class="big-question">For preparing and leading the class. For catechist use only.</p>

<h3>Class Summary</h3>

<p><strong>Estimated Duration:</strong> 60 minutes</p>
<p><strong>Central Theme:</strong> Confirmation as the sacrament that completes Baptism and gives a special anointing of the Holy Spirit.</p>
<p><strong>Objectives:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Understand the relationship between Baptism and Confirmation.</li>
<li>Discover the meaning of "spiritual consecration" through anointing.</li>
<li>Know the seven gifts of the Holy Spirit.</li>
<li>Value the apostolic mission that Confirmation confers.</li>
<li>Understand the bishop's role as ordinary minister.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Key Verse:</strong> "Receive the Holy Spirit. If you forgive the sins of any, they are forgiven them" (John 20:22-23)</p>
<p><strong>Catechism References:</strong> CCC 1285-1321</p>

</section>

